#70405
"At the Base of an Oak Tree"
"You stand in a small hollow in the woods, at the center of which stand a large

oak tree.  The ground about the base is littered in acorn fragments, chewed

through by foraging animals long ago.  Gnarled oak roots occasionally break

the uniform surface of the ground.  Dense vegetation surrounds the hollow on

all sides except the east.  In that direction the vegetation is thin enough to

push through and reach what seems to be a trail.

"
